# Build context exclusions, shared by every image built from the repo root
# (deploy/runner/Dockerfile, mcp_server/Dockerfile). docker/agents/build.sh
# builds from its own docker/agents/build-context/ dir, so it is unaffected.
#
# Two jobs here: keep credentials out of the context entirely (a build context
# is uploaded to the daemon and anything in it can end up in a layer), and keep
# the ~1.5G of local state out so builds don't spend minutes on the upload.
#
# Everything the Dockerfiles COPY must stay OUT of this file: pyproject.toml,
# uv.lock, main.py, agents.yaml, sregym/, mcp_server/, clients/, logger/,
# llm_backend/, atif_converter/, docker/, scripts/, SREGym-applications/.

# --- Credentials. Never in a build context. ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
provisioner_ssh_key
provisioner_ssh_key.pub
kubeconfig.yaml
context.json
*.login.info.txt
sregym/config.yml
scripts/ansible/inventory.yml

# --- Local state: large, machine-specific, regenerated in-image. ---
.git
**/.git
.venv
venv/
env/
ENV/
.runtime/
results/
logs/
trace_output/
metrics_output/
cache_dir/
data/
demos/
wandb/
taskweaver_proj/
docker/agents/build-context/
sregym/observer/telemetry_data_*/
dataset/functional/**/groundtruth/
dataset/functional/**/log/
dataset/functional/**/metric/
dataset/functional/**/trace/
sregym/conductor/tasklist.yml

# --- Python / test caches. ---
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
build/
dist/

# --- Dev-only trees. Not COPY'd by any Dockerfile; --no-dev skips their deps. ---
tests/
docs/
python-database/

# --- Editor / agent tooling. ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.cursor/
.kiro/
.pi/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.DS_Store
